     2	
     3	Status: resolved
     4	Blocked by: —
     5	
     6	Build the whole export as pure logic over value types, with one thin SwiftData-reading
     7	collector. No UI in this ticket.
     8	
     9	## Files
    10	
    11	- `WorkoutTracker/Domain/ExportSnapshot.swift` — `Codable` value types mirroring the export
    12	  shape in `../spec.md` (JSON section). Value types only: no `@Model` reference escapes here.
    13	- `WorkoutTracker/Domain/ExportCollector.swift` — builds an `ExportSnapshot` from a
    14	  `ModelContext`. Touches SwiftData, imports no UI.
    15	- `WorkoutTracker/Domain/ExportCSV.swift` — pure `ExportSnapshot → String` renderer.
    16	- `WorkoutTracker/Domain/ExportJSON.swift` — pure `ExportSnapshot → Data` encoder.
    17	- `WorkoutTrackerTests/ExportTests.swift`
    18	
    19	## Acceptance criteria
    20	
    21	- [x] `ExportSnapshot` is `Codable` and round-trips: `decode(encode(x)) == x` for a snapshot
    22	      exercising every optional (no gym, no machine, free-weight tag, draft set, active workout).
    23	- [x] **D28** — the collector includes every user-created exercise/model plus exactly those
    24	      seeded rows referenced by machines, entry snapshots, template items, gym-exercise memory
    25	      or rest overrides. A store with the 1877-row seeded catalog and one logged workout
    26	      exports at most a handful of catalog rows.
    27	- [x] **D29** — every set carries `weight`, `unit`, `weightKg`; no value in either format is a
    28	      converted display value and no `≈` appears anywhere.
    29	- [x] **D30** — draft sets, zero-completed-set entries and an unfinished workout all appear,
    30	      flagged.
    31	- [x] **D31** — every timestamp is ISO 8601 with a UTC offset; the formatter is injectable so
    32	      tests pin a fixed timezone.
    33	- [x] **D32** — CSV is RFC 4180: CRLF terminators, UTF-8 BOM, fields containing `"`, `,`, CR or
    34	      LF quoted with inner quotes doubled. Verbatim user text (no formula-injection prefixing).
    35	- [x] CSV rows are ordered workout `startedAt` → workout id → entry `order` → set `order`, and
    36	      the header row matches the 27 columns in `../spec.md` exactly, in order.
    37	- [x] CSV context columns read entry snapshots (D23), never live rows. A test renames a gym
    38	      after logging and asserts the exported row keeps the old name.
    39	- [x] JSON is pretty-printed with sorted keys and omits nil optionals rather than emitting
    40	      `null`; `schemaVersion` is 1.
    41	- [x] Numbers serialize locale-independently (`.` separator) — a test runs under a comma-decimal
    42	      locale.
    43	- [x] Empty store exports a header-only CSV and a JSON with empty collections, not an error.
    44	
    45	## Resolution (2026-08-11)
    46	
    47	Landed as `Domain/ExportSnapshot.swift` (value types + `ExportDateFormat`),
    48	`Domain/ExportCollector.swift` (the one SwiftData reader), `Domain/ExportCSV.swift`,
    49	`Domain/ExportJSON.swift`, `Domain/ExportFile.swift` (naming/staging, moved here from ticket 02
    50	because a filename is part of the format). Tests: `WorkoutTrackerTests/ExportTests.swift`
    51	(encoders) with the RFC 4180 reader in `ExportTestSupport.swift`.
    52	
    53	Two things worth knowing:
    54	
    55	- Timestamps are formatted **once, at collection time**, and live in the snapshot as strings.
    56	  Formatting per renderer would let the two files disagree, and an ISO 8601 `Date` round-trip
    57	  truncates sub-second precision, so `decode(encode(x)) == x` would have been false.
    58	- D28 is deliberately **non-transitive**: a referenced model's `exerciseIDs` may name exercises
    59	  nothing else references, and following those links drags in much of the catalog.
