A second concrete file-format defect surfaced: Swift treats `"\r\n"` as one `Character`, so the writer’s “contains CR or LF” predicate misses a CRLF pair. A Windows-style newline inside notes is emitted unquoted and becomes a real row boundary, violating D32 and corrupting strict CSV parsing. The existing tests cover lone `\n`, not this case. I’m folding this and the catalog-link loss into the final ranked review now.
